 "example_item": "POLICY. A rule applies only if its jurisdiction covers the debtor country and its condition holds.\nWhen applicable rules prescribe different values: (1) the higher authority prevails (Regulator > Payment scheme > Market-practice group > Bank policy); (2) at equal authority, the narrower jurisdiction prevails; (3) at equal authority and jurisdiction, the later effective date prevails; (4) if still tied, answer ESCALATE.\nMESSAGE. pacs.008; debtor country SG; currency EUR; amount 250000.\nRULES (listed in no particular order).\nR1 [Regulator; jurisdiction: all countries; effective 2024-07-01; condition: currency is EUR] Charge bearer must be CRED.\nR2 [Market-practice group; jurisdiction: all countries; effective 2023-07-01] Charge bearer must be SHAR.\nR3 [Regulator; jurisdiction: US, CA, BR; effective 2025-10-01; condition: currency is EUR] Charge bearer must be SHAR.\nQUESTION. Which charge-bearer value must be used (DEBT, CRED, SHAR, SLEV or ESCALATE)?",
